WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:06.490
After MTV's Jackass became a rowdy cultural
phenomenon, thousands of younger men who were

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:08.880
inspired by their pranks tried to do the same
thing.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:13.670
The dust has since cleared, and Roman Atwood
has emerged as the most successful Jackass

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:14.670
disciple.

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:19.110
The Columbus, Ohio resident owns two mega-popular
YouTube channels through which he's performed

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:23.510
pranks all over the world and work with legends
like Steve-O and The Dudesons.

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:27.789
He's also taken his viral videos to the big
screen, producing a full-length movie called

00:00:27.789 --> 00:00:29.450
Natural Born Pranksters.

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:33.950
But if you think Roman Atwood is just an overnight
success who gets paid to goof around on camera

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:35.840
all day, you couldn't be more wrong.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:39.120
Let's find out about Roman Atwood before all
the fame...

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:40.560
It all begins

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:45.770
On May 28, 1983, Roman Atwood was born in
Millersport, Ohio.

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:49.830
His relationship with the camera started not
long after, and he soon became obsessed with

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:51.969
shooting and editing "stupid videos."

00:00:51.969 --> 00:00:55.371
"I saved up like $300 bucks and bought my
first camera when I was like a kid, and the

00:00:55.371 --> 00:00:58.370
only reason I ever started filming was I wanted
things to edit.

00:00:58.370 --> 00:00:59.370
I love to edit."

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:04.059
By junior high, he graduated to shooting and
editing sketch comedy videos with his friends.

00:01:04.059 --> 00:01:07.170
That's around the time when he really checked
out emotionally with school.

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:11.369
He claims that he just couldn't see how his
classes would prepare him for a world of video,

00:01:11.369 --> 00:01:13.109
and often fell asleep in the seat.

00:01:13.109 --> 00:01:17.369
As Atwood once put it, "I didn't need to learn
about World War II to make these videos."

00:01:17.369 --> 00:01:23.079
He also fell in love with a fellow student
named Shanna Reilly, whom he married in 2001,

00:01:23.079 --> 00:01:25.159
five months after they graduated.

00:01:25.159 --> 00:01:29.590
Having no more interest in college than high
school, Atwood opted out of higher education,

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:33.340
despite his teachers' warning that he'd make
nothing of his life if he didn't get a bachelor's.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:34.590
Rough times

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:39.429
To support his new wife and video-making obsession,
Atwood took a job working in his family's

00:01:39.429 --> 00:01:44.159
business and felt discouraged by the time
spent away from his video-making habits.

00:01:44.159 --> 00:01:47.850
Despite his depression, he still made videos
on the side with his friends and brother,

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:52.560
Dale Atwood, and worked on various film projects
and commercials around Columbus.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:57.499
One such project was a DVD of Atwood and his
friends - collectively called The Nerd Herd

00:01:57.499 --> 00:02:02.979
- doing Jackass-style comedy In 2006, Atwood
and his brother traveled around the country

00:02:02.979 --> 00:02:05.509
with the Warped Tour, selling hundreds of
copies.

00:02:05.509 --> 00:02:10.290
A year after that, Atwood got what he believed
would be his big break, when a friend invited

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:12.620
him out to Los Angeles to help work on a movie.

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:17.110
However, when he arrived on set, the young
videographer realized it was not what he'd

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:19.470
hoped: "It was this little low-budget thing,
not a

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:20.470
movie at all."

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:25.660
Even still, Atwood seemed to be gaining more
momentum in his professional life than before.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:27.860
Unfortunately, his personal life was crumbling.

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:32.120
While on his LA trip, his wife reportedly
cheated on him with a guy who had helped Atwood

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:33.400
with his videos.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:38.950
Atwood didn't find out until 2008, and describes
it as "the worst, most devastating time in

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:39.950
[his] life."

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:44.530
Fortunately, bad situations can inspire good
creativity — He saw the divorce as a wake-up

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:49.360
call to completely re-dedicate himself to
his passion of comedy and video production.

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:51.700
The realization that changed everything

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:55.640
In 2010, he and his friends created Roman
Atwood's Sketch Empire.

00:02:55.640 --> 00:03:00.040
For almost two years, the group uploaded a
video every Tuesday, with the hope of someday

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:01.710
having one go viral.

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:04.480
Despite their high hopes, the videos didn't
catch on.

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:08.440
Finally, Atwood got the idea to shoot a prank
video where they pretended to pour an empty

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:10.900
water cooler on unsuspecting pedestrians.

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:15.470
Even though the people never got wet, their
reactions earned the prank video more views

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:16.880
than all others combined.

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:20.660
While they continued uploading new sketch
videos after the cooler prank, the feedback

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:25.430
was almost completely negative, so he decided
to turn it into a full-blown prank channel.

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:29.569
The group got their first truly viral video
when they started "pee pranks," where they'd

00:03:29.569 --> 00:03:34.040
pretend to urinate on the street, and people
were fooled, even the police, and the YouTube

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:35.250
views climbed upward.

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:40.350
Viewers really seemed to love the police pranking
part, so somewhere along the way, Atwood rebranded

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:44.810
the Sketch Empire YouTube account as simply
RomanAtwood.

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:46.069
Viral superstardom

00:03:46.069 --> 00:03:50.460
Just as his name came into internet fame,
Atwood's personal life began improving as

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:51.460
well.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:55.060
He started dating Britney Smith, who soon
started appearing in his videos as well.

00:03:55.060 --> 00:04:00.319
By 2011, "pee pranks" had amassed millions
of views, and just a year later, Atwood quit

00:04:00.319 --> 00:04:03.420
the family business to pursue prank videos
full-time.

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:07.790
His girlfriend later became an Internet star
in her own right as well, when Atwood posted

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:09.150
"Anniversary Prank Backfires!!"

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:13.600
He was trying to prank her on their five-year
anniversary by pretending he had cheated,

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:18.060
but she saw the camera beforehand and pranked
him back by pretending she had cheated too.

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:19.780
In the end, the joke was on him.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:21.070
"Oh My God."

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:24.180
"I thought you were going to propose."

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:29.789
The video was insanely popular, clocking in
over 86 million views, and was a big part

00:04:29.789 --> 00:04:33.580
of a full-on girlfriend pranking trend he's
carried on over the years since.

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:35.080
"It’s not funny."

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:36.080
"I know."

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:37.580
"It’s not funny."

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:38.580
"It’s…

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:39.939
It’s kinda funny."

00:04:39.939 --> 00:04:44.000
Every year seems to get better and better
for Atwood, as he continues cranking out videos

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:46.900
for his channels and even promotes his Smile
More store.

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:51.699
Keep your eyes peeled, because another viral
prank is almost certainly coming along very

00:04:51.699 --> 00:04:52.699
soon.

00:04:52.699 --> 00:04:53.699
Thanks for watching!

00:04:53.699 --> 00:04:56.150
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:58.509
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

